Subject: drm/nouveau/nv17_fence: don't report a sync that never happened

nv17_fence_sync() chains a GPU semaphore across two channels: the previous
channel acquires value+0 and releases value+1, the new channel acquires
value+1 and releases value+2. The semaphore is a single shared location and
priv->sequence is the global counter that drives it, so the two have to stay
in step.

The counter was advanced before anything was emitted, each emission was
conditional on its own PUSH_WAIT succeeding, and the function returned 0
regardless:

	value = priv->sequence;
	priv->sequence += 2;
	ret = PUSH_WAIT(ppush, 5);
	if (!ret) { ...acquire value+0, release value+1...  }
	if (!ret && !(ret = PUSH_WAIT(npush, 5))) { ...value+1, value+2... }
	return 0;

If either PUSH_WAIT fails the counter has still moved, so the semaphore is
left permanently behind it, and the next sync emits an ACQUIRE for a value
the semaphore will never reach. The channel that executes that acquire then
sits with its pushbuf fully fetched (GET == PUT), PGRAPH idle and its fence
never signalled -- indefinitely, with nothing logged anywhere. Captured on a
GeForce 7600 GS:

  STALL ch1 gr:status=00000000 ctxctl=0000e001 | put=00521f34 get=00521f34
  fence deadline: want seq 2, engine at 0 -> engine is genuinely behind

repeated identically while a second channel ran normally beside it.

Returning 0 also tells nouveau_fence_sync() the GPU side is handled, so it
skips the dma_fence_wait() fallback that would otherwise have been correct.

Reserve room on both channels before consuming a sequence value, and return
the error. The caller then falls back to a CPU wait, which is slower and
always right.

NOTE: this does not fix every stall on this hardware. A second, distinct mode
remains, in which PGRAPH is busy, GET is behind PUT and not advancing, and
CTX_CONTROL bit 0 is clear -- an engine hung mid-work rather than a channel
blocked on a semaphore. That one is untouched by this patch.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nv17_fence.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nv17_fence.c
@@ nv17_fence_sync()
-	spin_lock(&priv->lock);
-	value = priv->sequence;
-	priv->sequence += 2;
-	spin_unlock(&priv->lock);
-
-	ret = PUSH_WAIT(ppush, 5);
-	if (!ret) {
-		...emit on prev...
-	}
-	if (!ret && !(ret = PUSH_WAIT(npush, 5))) {
-		...emit on chan...
-	}
-	mutex_unlock(&cli->mutex);
-	return 0;
+	ret = PUSH_WAIT(ppush, 5);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = PUSH_WAIT(npush, 5);
+	if (ret) {
+		mutex_unlock(&cli->mutex);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
+	spin_lock(&priv->lock);
+	value = priv->sequence;
+	priv->sequence += 2;
+	spin_unlock(&priv->lock);
+
+	...emit on prev, then on chan, unconditionally...
+	mutex_unlock(&cli->mutex);
+	return 0;
